.TH N900 7 "2026-11-17" "N900 Resurrection" "Miscellaneous Information"
.SH NAME
n900 \- software for the Nokia N900 from the N900 Resurrection project
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Nokia N900 runs Maemo 5 "Fremantle" (armel, glibc 2.5). This project builds modern software for it and serves it as an apt repository.
Every package installs under
.IR /opt/<package> ,
with a link in
.I /usr/bin
for the commands; the manual pages are in
.IR /opt/<package>/share/man ,
the documentation and the licence in
.IR /opt/<package>/share/doc/<package> .
.SH REPOSITORY
The source line (in
.IR /etc/apt/sources.list.d/n900.list ):
.PP
.RS
deb https://n900-resurrection.github.io/n900-repository fremantle main
.RE
.PP
The apt of the phone speaks TLS 1.0 only, so the packages
.B curl
and
.B apt\-transport\-curl
(see
.BR apt\-transport\-curl (8))
are installed by hand first, with
.BR "dpkg \-i" .
They need
.B bash3
and
.B coreutils\-gnu
from Extras. The repository is not signed yet.
The Application Manager can add it from an install file.
.SH THE MANUAL PAGES
The BusyBox
.B man
of the phone cannot format a page (it needs
.BR nroff ).
The package
.B mandoc
provides
.BR man ,
.B apropos
and
.BR whatis .
The search path is set at login by
.IR /etc/profile.d/mandoc.sh ,
so open a new terminal after the installation. The index for
.B apropos
is rebuilt by
.B mandoc\-update
(run it as root after you install a package with
.B dpkg \-i
or with the Application Manager;
.B apt\-get
does it by itself).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (1),
.BR apt\-transport\-curl (8),
.BR man (1),
.BR mandoc (1)
.PP
The web site, with the package catalogue and the guide: https://n900-resurrection.github.io
.br
The sources: https://github.com/n900-resurrection
